          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %strong tangent category
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is an approximation to the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} tangent (∞,1)-category
            in ordinary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
          %p For the moment see there for further motivation.
          %p
            The tangent category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_C
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is effectively the
            %em fiberwise abelianization
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain+fibration"} codomain fibration
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cod
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi I
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cod : [I,C] \to C
          %p
            we may think of it as obtained from the codomain fibration by replacing each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
            fiber
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi I
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [I,C]_A = C/A
            by the corresponding category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+objects"} group objects
            and restricting the morphisms such as to respect the abelian group object structure.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            with
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            %strong tangent category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_C
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is the category whose
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"}> object
                s are pairs
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒜
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,\mathcal{A})
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Ob
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in Ob(C)
                and with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒜
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck+module"} Beck module
                over
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
                in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/A
              %p
                notice that for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℬ
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B} \to B
                an object in the overcategory that is equipped with the structure of an abelian group object – notably with a product
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi prod
                        %mi ℬ
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℬ
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mi B
                      %mi ℬ
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℬ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} prod_{\mathcal{B}} : \mathcal{B} \times_B \mathcal{B} \to  \mathcal{B}
                – and for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon A \to B
                any morphism in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mi ℬ
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mi B
                      %mi ℬ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^* \mathcal{B} \coloneqq A \times_B \mathcal{B}
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is naturally equipped with the structure of an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal to
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/A
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"}> morphism
                s
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒻
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒜
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℬ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f, \mathcal{f}) : (A,\mathcal{A}) \to (B, \mathcal{B})
                are commuting squares
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi 𝒜
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mi 𝒻
                            %mtd
                              %mi ℬ
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi A
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mi f
                            %mtd
                              %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \\mathcal{A} &amp;\stackrel{\mathcal{f}}{\to}&amp; \mathcal{B}
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                      \\\
                      A &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; B
                      }
              %p
                such that the induced morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒜
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mi ℬ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A} \to f^*\mathcal{B}
                is a morphism of abelian group objects in
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/A
            %li
              %p
                composition of morphisms is given in the evident way by
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒻
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∘
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒻
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ∘
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒻
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ∘
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒻
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f_2, \mathcal{f}_2) \circ (f_1, \mathcal{f}_1) = (f_2 \circ f_1, \mathcal{f}_2 \circ \mathcal{f}_1)
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#general General
          %p
            There is an evident
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : T_C \to C
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain+fibration"} codomain fibration
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒜
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi 𝒻
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℬ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                    %mo )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ↦
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  p
                  \\;\;:
                  \\;\;
                  \\left(
                  \\array{
                  \\mathcal{A} &amp;\stackrel{\mathcal{f}}{\to}&amp; \mathcal{B}
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  A &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; B
                  }
                  \\right)
                  \\;\;
                  \\mapsto
                  \\;\;
                  (A \stackrel{f}{\to} B)
                  \\,.
          %p
            The fiber over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Id
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id_A
            of this functor is the category of abelian group objects in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi C
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi A
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Ab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (T_C)_A \simeq Ab(C/A)
                  \\,.
          %p
            There is also another functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q : T_C \to C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain+cofibration"} domain cofibration
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒜
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi 𝒻
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℬ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                    %mo )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ↦
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒻
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  q
                  \\;\;:
                  \\;\;
                  \\left(
                  \\array{
                  \\mathcal{A} &amp;\stackrel{\mathcal{f}}{\to}&amp; \mathcal{B}
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  A &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; B
                  }
                  \\right)
                  \\;\;
                  \\mapsto
                  \\;\;
                  (\mathcal{A} \stackrel{\mathcal{f}}{\to} \mathcal{B})
                  \\,,
          %p where we first forget the abelian group object structure and then project onto the domains.
          %blockquote
            %p
              (we should be claiming that this functor has a left adjoint which is a section and computes the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+differentials"} Kähler differentials
              of objects in
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %h3#of_a_site Of a site
          %p
            We discuss morphisms of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
          %blockquote
            %p check
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be a category with
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limit"} finite limit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_C \to C
            be its tangent category.
          %p
            There is then the 0-section
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i : C \to T_C
            which sends
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to the terminal object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Id
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id : A\to A
            in the overcategory, equipped, necessarily, with the trivial group structure. This exhibits
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_C
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi C
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi p
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Id
                    %mi C
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (C \stackrel{i}{\to} T_C \stackrel{p}{\to} C) = Id_C
                  \\,.
          %p
            Assume now that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}
            has
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
          %p
            Equip
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi C
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T_C)^{op}
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f_i : U_i \to U\}
            is a cover in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi C
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T_C)^{op}
            precisely if its image
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{p(f_i) : p(U_i) \to p(U)\}
            is a cover in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}
          %p
            Then the 0-section
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi C
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op} \to (T_C)^{op}
            preserves covers.
          %p
            We claim it also preserves limits: i.e. that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i : C \to T_C
            preserves
            = succeed "s:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
          %p
            let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi K
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : K \to C
            be a diagram and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi lim
                    %mo →
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim_\to F
            its colimit in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            be any cocone under
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \circ F
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            to that cocone we find that there is a unique morphism of cocones
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi lim
                    %mo →
                  %mi F
                  %mo →
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Q
